.end
Lib Copy and Lib Cut work like Copy and Cut (the same list of four choices
and the same highlight) and put the area into the library of the Tools menu
as well as into the clipboard; Lib Paste pastes an entry of the library at the
cursor, without changing the clipboard.
.h4 The Ctrl letters
.table 11 21 22
Key | What it does | Described in
{k:Ctrl-A} | Append a block, same format | {x:edit-append}
{k:Ctrl-B} | Bold on or off | {x:edit-typing}
{k:Ctrl-C} | Spell check of the word | {n:spell}
{k:Ctrl-D} | Delete the word | {x:edit-deleting}
{k:Ctrl-E} | The format of the block | {n:format}
{k:Ctrl-F} | The Alt commands menu | {x:edit-altmenu}
{k:Ctrl-G} | The text indent character | {x:edit-typing}
{k:Ctrl-H} | Hanging indent | {x:edit-typing}
{k:Ctrl-I} | Tab, in both versions; italics is {k:Alt-I} | {x:edit-typing}
{k:Ctrl-K} | Cut the block | {x:edit-cut}
{k:Ctrl-L} | Cut the section | {x:edit-cut}
{k:Ctrl-N} | Normal text | {x:edit-typing}
{k:Ctrl-O} | Append a block, global format | {x:edit-append}
{k:Ctrl-P} | Print, Final | {n:print}
{k:Ctrl-Q} | Quit | {x:edit-b-quit}
{k:Ctrl-R} | Retrieve | {n:file}
{k:Ctrl-S} | Save | {n:file}
{k:Ctrl-T} | Thesaurus for the word | {n:spell}
{k:Ctrl-U} | Underscore on or off | {x:edit-typing}
{k:Ctrl-V} | Split the block | {x:edit-b-split}
{k:Ctrl-W} | Equation editor: view | {n:equations}
{k:Ctrl-X} | Cut text | {x:edit-cut}
{k:Ctrl-Y} | Split the section | {x:edit-b-split}
{k:Ctrl-Z} | Undo (also {k:Ctrl-/}) | {x:edit-b-undo}
{k:Ctrl-^} | Section edit on or off | {x:edit-b-section}
.end
{k:Ctrl-C} checks the spelling of the word at the cursor and {k:Ctrl-T} shows
synonyms of it ({n:spell}).  {k:Ctrl-Shift-Space} is not a letter: it types a
nonbreaking space ({n:edit-nbsp}).  {k:Ctrl-W} works in the editor of an
equation.  The
keys {k:Ctrl-M} and {k:Ctrl-J} are Enter, and {k:Ctrl-I} is Tab.  In the
terminal version {k:Ctrl-C}, {k:Ctrl-S}, {k:Ctrl-Q} and {k:Ctrl-Z} are keys of the Editor:
they neither stop the program nor freeze the screen.
